  "question": {
    "text": "Three charges $-q_1,+q_2$ and $-q_3$ are placed as shown in the figure. The $x$-component of the force on $-q_1$ is proportional to\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3PD4GSG2iGM4h9jlamuimPubBFv1SfxQFlwYEKHcKS0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LjuBh",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\cos \\theta$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9rtb0",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\sin \\theta$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CQG0G",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\cos \\theta$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iYn2m",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\sin \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The force body diagram\n$F_1=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0} \\cdot \\frac{q_1 q_3}{a^2}$         $\\mathrm{F}_2=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{q}_1 \\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}$   <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/KbKrw2Or0F6AgX2g0bnbQ98qP8NPvJXhClzs9jkajrs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{X}}=\\mathrm{F}_1 \\sin \\theta+\\mathrm{F}_2=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0}\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\sin \\theta+\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_1}{\\mathrm{~b}_2}\\right] \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{X}} \\propto\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_3}{\\mathrm{a}^2} \\sin \\theta+\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
